# direnv configuration — convenience only, never load-bearing.
#
# `make` and env/scripts/run{python,julia,stata,notebook} work with direnv
# absent, and must keep working: a project generated from this template is a
# replication package, and reviewers will not have direnv installed. Nothing in
# the reproduction path may depend on this file.
#
# What it buys: a bare `python` in this directory — in a terminal, or in Emacs
# via envrc.el — behaves like `env/scripts/runpython`, including the Julia
# bridge. Without it, an interactive `python` gets the wrong interpreter and none
# of the JULIA_* wiring, which is a quiet way to get wrong answers.
#
# Run `direnv allow` once after cloning, and again after editing this file.
#
# Ported from fire 2026-08-19. env/env.sh here has named .envrc in its own
# comments since it was written — "Sourced by env/scripts/run{...} and by
# .envrc" — while no such file existed, so the template documented a file it did
# not ship and every generated project inherited the same gap.

# env/env.sh also sources env/local.sh (gitignored) if present, so machine-local
# settings like DATA_DIR reach `make` and direnv alike. Nothing goes here.
source env/env.sh

if [[ -n "$REPRO_VENV" ]]; then
  PATH_add "$REPRO_VENV/bin"
else
  log_status "no .venv yet — run 'make environment'"
fi
